{% extends "page.twig" %}

{#
	A case study composes from the same section stack as a page, so the loop in
	page.twig is the whole body. `work` is registered with the same `sections`
	field group for exactly this reason.

	If work-single ever needs something a page can't express, add a section
	layout — not a second loop.

	The one thing below the stack is next-project, which is *not* a section: it
	is derived from the query, has no ACF row behind it, and must not be
	reorderable. It sits here rather than in a layout for the same reason
	breadcrumbs and pagination do.

	Older first — the archive reads newest to oldest, so the project after this
	one is the older one. The oldest case study has nothing older, so it falls
	back to the newer sibling, which closes the loop instead of dead-ending.
#}

{% block content %}
	{{ parent() }}

	{% include 'partials/ui/next-project.twig' with {
		project: post.prev ?: post.next
	} only %}
{% endblock %}
